* nixie_rev2 simulation-only models
* These models are intentionally local and documented approximations.
* They are suitable for topology bring-up, not final tolerance or stress sign-off.

.model ES2J_APPROX D(Is=5n N=1.8 Rs=0.12 Cjo=25p M=0.33 Vj=0.7 Tt=35n Bv=600 Ibv=10u)
.model NCD0603R1_APPROX D(Is=1e-18 N=2 Rs=10 Cjo=20p Bv=5 Ibv=10u)

.subckt PTC_FUSE_1A_APPROX P N
RFUSE P N 0.055
.ends PTC_FUSE_1A_APPROX

.subckt 2N7002_APPROX D G S
MCHANNEL D G S S 2N7002_CORE
.model 2N7002_CORE NMOS(Level=1 Vto=1.6 Kp=0.07 Lambda=0.02 Rd=1 Rs=1 Cgso=10p Cgdo=5p Cbd=10p Cbs=10p)
.ends 2N7002_APPROX

* Five-pin order follows the MCP6001-OT symbol: OUT, VSS, IN+, IN-, VDD.
* The 1 kHz dominant pole with gain 1000 approximates a 1 MHz gain-bandwidth product.
.subckt MCP6001_APPROX OUT VSS INP INN VDD
RINP INP VSS 1T
RINN INN VSS 1T
BGAIN NRAW VSS V={0.5*V(VDD,VSS)*(1+tanh(400*V(INP,INN)))}
RDOM NRAW NPOLE 10k
CDOM NPOLE VSS 15.9n
ROUT NPOLE OUT 50
COUT OUT VSS 10p
.ends MCP6001_APPROX

* TDK ATB322524-0110-T000 transformer approximation from the manufacturer data.
* Defaults use 7 uH primary inductance, 1:10.2 turns ratio, and the published
* maximum primary/secondary DCR values of 0.5/60 ohm. K=0.9710083 corresponds to
* the published 0.4 uH maximum primary-referred leakage inductance.
* Physical mapping is 1=P1, 4=P2, 2=S1, 3=S2. The datasheet has no polarity
* dots, so the model assumes physical pins 1 and 2 are the in-phase starts.
.subckt ATB322524_0110_APPROX P1 P2 S1 S2 params: LPRI=7u NTR=10.2 RPRI=0.5 RSEC=60 KCOUP=0.9710083
RPRI_E P1 NP {RPRI}
LPRIMARY NP P2 {LPRI}
RSEC_E S1 NS {RSEC}
LSECONDARY NS S2 {LPRI*NTR*NTR}
KXFMR LPRIMARY LSECONDARY {KCOUP}
.ends ATB322524_0110_APPROX

* Behavioral XL6007 topology model.
* It models a 400 kHz PWM-controlled 0.12 ohm low-side switch, a 1.25 V
* feedback target, an approximate 50 ms soft-start, 50 pF switch capacitance,
* and a 60 V switch-node protection clamp. The soft-start timing and clamp
* characteristic are simulation assumptions because the datasheet does not
* specify them. A clock-reset latch approximates the published 2 A cycle
* current limit. Current-mode compensation, thermal behavior, and detailed
* losses are not modeled.
.subckt XL6007_APPROX EN VIN FB NC SW1 SW2 GND1 GND2
RSW_JOIN SW1 SW2 1m
RGND_JOIN GND1 GND2 1m
RFB_BIAS FB GND1 100Meg
REN_BIAS EN GND1 10Meg
RNC NC GND1 1Gig
RQUIESCENT VIN GND1 2.4k
RSS EN SS 500k
CSS SS GND1 100n
VRAMP RAMP GND1 PULSE(0 1 0 2.498u 1n 1n 2.5u)
BDUTY DUTY GND1 V={0.45*(1+tanh(1.18+20*(1.25-V(FB,GND1))))*min(1,max(0,V(SS,GND1)/5))}
BPWM CTRL GND1 V={5*(0.5+0.5*tanh(100*(V(EN,GND1)-1.4)))*(0.5+0.5*tanh(100*(V(VIN,GND1)-3.6)))*(0.5+0.5*tanh(100*(V(DUTY,GND1)-V(RAMP,GND1))))}
RSENSE SW1 NSW 1m
BLATCH QLIM GND1 I={V(RAMP,GND1)<0.01 ? V(QLIM,GND1) : (V(SW1,NSW)>2m ? V(QLIM,GND1)-5 : 0)}
CLATCH QLIM GND1 100p
BGATE GATE GND1 V={V(CTRL,GND1)*(0.5+0.5*tanh(100*(2.5-V(QLIM,GND1))))}
SPOWER NSW GND1 GATE GND1 XL6007_SW
COSS SW1 GND1 50p
DBODY GND1 SW1 XL6007_BODY
.model XL6007_SW SW(Ron=0.12 Roff=100Meg Vt=2.5 Vh=0.1)
.model XL6007_BODY D(Is=1n N=1.5 Rs=0.1 Cjo=20p Bv=60 Ibv=1m)
.ends XL6007_APPROX
